cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the accompanying paper (in preparation)."

title: "Snow Removal for Spinning LiDAR Point Clouds with Surface-Veto Outlier Removal"

abstract: >-
  SVOR detects and removes snowfall-induced noise from mechanical spinning
  LiDAR point clouds per point, at frame rate, on CPU, without training, GPU or
  learned weights. It combines the intensity- and distance-aware statistical
  threshold of IDSOR (Yan & Bengtsson, 2026), a per-point intensity score fused
  with a normalised height-above-ground term, and a zero-intensity surface veto
  that rejects weak returns attached to a bright surface. The algorithm core is
  ROS-agnostic and ships as a library with an offline CLI; a separate ROS 2
  package wraps it as a point-cloud node. Both paths produce bit-identical
  detections, which is enforced by a byte-exact regression against a released
  reference output.

references:
  - type: article
    title: "IDSOR: Intensity- and Distance-Aware Statistical Outlier Removal for Weather-Robust LiDAR Point Clouds"
